{
  "_comment": [
    "cadtui-locale-option-keywords.issue: the INTERNATIONAL (English) keyword of",
    "each LOCAL (fr_FR) option keyword harvested by the optkw probe. Both runners",
    "are French installs, so the English side is taken from the vendors' English",
    "command reference (url, per command), paired by POSITION and MEANING with",
    "the harvested prompt. 'local' repeats the harvest so the converter can refuse",
    "a pairing whose harvest has moved; 'international' is aligned with it, and",
    "null means NOT paired: the English documentation does not settle it, so it",
    "is left to measure on an English install (never guessed).",
    "The international strings are the documented option labels as the reference",
    "writes them (BricsCAD's reference shows the prompt's capitals, e.g. mEthod;",
    "Autodesk's shows plain headings, e.g. Method) -- not a measured English prompt.",
    "Used by: scripts/cadtui-optkw-to-sexp.py --pair (see its docstring)."
  ],
